-- title:
--   Exceptional multidegree zero implies local triviality on the uv=varpi^e resolution
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with $\mathfrak m_O=(\varpi)$, let $e\ge 1$, let $\pi_X:X\to\operatorname{Spec}O$ be separated, let $x\in U\subseteq X$ with $U$ open, and let $f:U\to\operatorname{Spec}\bigl(O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1-\varpi^{e})\bigr)$ be locally of finite type and formally unramified, compatible with the structure morphisms ($f$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $O\to O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1-\varpi^{e})$ equals the inclusion of $U$ followed by $\pi_X$), and such that a point $y\in U$ has $f(y)$ in the union of the basic opens of the two coordinates exactly when $y\neq x$. Write $Y$ for the fibre product of $f$ with `Resolution.toCrossing` $\varpi\,e$ (the toric resolution of $uv=\varpi^{e}$, glued from $e$ charts); assume the second projection is injective on the fibre of the first projection over $x$, that $Y$ is integral, and that some point of $Y$ maps outside the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}O$. Let $F_0,\dots,F_e$ be ideal sheaf data on the resolution, each invertible in the sense that locally on an affine basic open it is generated by a single non-zero-divisor, with $\prod_k F_k$ cut out by the image of $\varpi$ and $\prod_k F_k^{k}$ by the image of the coordinate $U(\varpi^e)$ (both via global sections of the relevant structure morphisms), all supports lying over the closed point of $O$, the supports of $F_k$ for $0<k<e$ lying over the vertex (both coordinates in the corresponding prime), $F_k$ and $F_{k+1}$ having a common support point for $k<e$, and every section $t$ of the resolution over $\operatorname{Spec}O$ whose closed point lies in the support of exactly one $F_{d}$ with $0<d<e$ being a closed immersion with invertible kernel and with $t.\ker\cdot\prod_k F_k^{\min(k,d)}$ generated by the pullback of a single element of $O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1-\varpi^{e})$. Let $\sigma_1,\dots,\sigma_m$ be sections of $Y$ over $\operatorname{Spec}O$ (each composed with the first projection and with $\pi_X$ giving the identity), with exponents $\mathrm{pos}_j,\mathrm{neg}_j$ and indices $0<d_j<e$ such that the closed point of $\sigma_j$ lies in the support of the pullback of $F_{d_j}$ to $Y$ and in no other; let $vp,vn:\{0,\dots,e\}\to\mathbb N$; and let $J_1,\dots,J_r$ be invertible ideal sheaf data on $Y$ whose supports are disjoint from the preimage of the closed point of $O$, with exponents $jp_i,jn_i$. Assume that for every $k$ with $0<k<e$ one has $\sum_{d_j=k}(\mathrm{pos}_j-\mathrm{neg}_j)+\bigl((vp-vn)(k-1)-2(vp-vn)(k)+(vp-vn)(k+1)\bigr)=0$. Then there is an open $V$ with $x\in V\le U$ such that the restriction to the preimage in $Y$ of $V$ of the tensor product, over $j$ and then over $i$ and then of the vertical factors, of $(\sigma_j.\ker^{\mathrm{pos}_j})^{\vee}\otimes \sigma_j.\ker^{\mathrm{neg}_j}$, of $(J_i^{jp_i})^{\vee}\otimes J_i^{jn_i}$, and of $\bigl(\prod_k (F_k|_Y)^{vp_k}\bigr)^{\vee}\otimes\prod_k (F_k|_Y)^{vn_k}$ — where an ideal sheaf is viewed as a module via the kernel of the unit mapping to the pushforward of the unit along the closed subscheme inclusion, and $(-)^{\vee}$ is the dual — admits an isomorphism to the unit module, i.e. the type of such isomorphisms is non-empty.
--
--   This is the local statement, at a single crossing, of divisorial descent along the minimal resolution of an $A_{e-1}$ singularity $uv=\varpi^{e}$ on an arithmetic surface: a line bundle written in terms of sections, horizontal ideals away from the special fibre and the exceptional components is trivial near the exceptional fibre as soon as its degree on every exceptional component vanishes, the vanishing being encoded by the discrete Laplacian condition on $vp-vn$ together with the section contributions. It is used by the corresponding global statements for resolved Deligne–Rapoport models, [`ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.DRResolvedModelCharts.exists_open_pullback_iso_unit_of_forall_exceptional_degree_eq_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.DRResolvedModelCharts.exists_open_pullback_iso_unit_of_forall_exceptional_degree_eq_zero) and [`ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.exists_isInvertible_and_pullback_toDR_iso_of_forall_exceptional_degree_eq_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.exists_isInvertible_and_pullback_toDR_iso_of_forall_exceptional_degree_eq_zero).
